      "content": "The idea of preserving a peak is a beautiful, tragic fantasy, but the truth is that stagnation is far more painful than the act of letting go. If you're already tasting mediocrity, you're already in the slow decline, and the only way to stop that descent is to choose a different path. Think of it not as giving up, but as making a decisive, powerful edit to your own narrative.",
